 {"id": "wine", "part": 3, "title": "Discovering wine cultivars", "short": "Clustering and PCA without labels",
  "lessons": [16, 17],
  "data": "178 wines from three grape cultivars grown in the same region of Italy (Forina et al.), shipped with scikit-learn as <code>load_wine</code>. Thirteen chemical measurements per wine: alcohol, malic acid, flavanoids, colour intensity, proline and more. The cultivar labels exist — but we hide them until the very end.",
  "goal": "Pretend we don't know the cultivars. Can PCA and clustering rediscover the three groups from the chemistry alone?",
  "skills": ["Standardising before PCA and k-means", "Explained variance", "Choosing k with the elbow and silhouette scores", "Checking clusters against hidden labels (adjusted Rand index)"],
  "steps": [
   ("Load the chemistry (and put the labels aside)", "",
    "import numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\nfrom sklearn.datasets import load_wine\nwine = load_wine(as_frame=True)\nX = wine.data                # 13 chemical measurements\nhidden_labels = wine.target  # we won't look at these until the end\nprint(X.shape)\nX.describe().loc[[\"mean\", \"std\"]].round(2)",
    [("X.shape", "load_wine(as_frame=True).data.")]),
   ("Standardise", "The features have wildly different scales (proline is in the hundreds, hue around 1). Standardise them so each counts equally (Lesson 17).",
    "from sklearn.preprocessing import StandardScaler\nZ = StandardScaler().fit_transform(X)  #TODO: standardise X\nprint(Z.mean(axis=0).round(2)[:4], Z.std(axis=0).round(2)[:4])",
    [("float(np.round(Z.std(axis=0).mean(), 6))", "StandardScaler().fit_transform(X) gives every column mean 0 and standard deviation 1.")]),
   ("PCA: how many directions matter?", "Fit PCA and look at the explained variance ratio of the first components.",
    "from sklearn.decomposition import PCA\npca = PCA().fit(Z)\nratio = pca.explained_variance_ratio_  #TODO: the explained variance ratio of every component\nprint(\"first five:\", ratio[:5].round(3))\nprint(\"cumulative:\", np.cumsum(ratio)[:5].round(3))",
    [("ratio[0]", "pca.explained_variance_ratio_."), ("np.cumsum(ratio)[1]", "The first two components together.")]),
   ("Look at the data in 2D", "Project onto the first two components and plot. Can you already see groups?",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nP = PCA(n_components=2).fit_transform(Z)\nplt.figure(figsize=(5, 4))\nplt.scatter(P[:, 0], P[:, 1], s=15, color=\"grey\")\nplt.xlabel(\"PC1\"); plt.ylabel(\"PC2\"); plt.title(\"178 wines, unlabelled\")\nplt.show()",
    []),
   ("Choose k", "Run k-means for k = 2 to 6 and compare inertia (elbow) and the silhouette score (Lesson 16).",
    "from sklearn.cluster import KMeans\nfrom sklearn.metrics import silhouette_score\nsil = {}\nfor k in range(2, 7):\n    km = KMeans(n_clusters=k, n_init=10, random_state=0).fit(Z)\n    sil[k] = silhouette_score(Z, km.labels_)  #TODO: the silhouette score of this clustering\n    print(f\"k={k}  inertia={km.inertia_:7.1f}  silhouette={sil[k]:.3f}\")\nbest_k = max(sil, key=sil.get)\nprint(\"best k by silhouette:\", best_k)",
    [("best_k", "silhouette_score(Z, km.labels_) for each k."), ("sil[3]", "Use n_init=10 and random_state=0.")]),
   ("Reveal the labels", "Now compare the clusters with the real cultivars. The adjusted Rand index (ARI) is 1 for a perfect match and about 0 for random clusters.",
    "from sklearn.metrics import adjusted_rand_score\nclusters = KMeans(n_clusters=best_k, n_init=10, random_state=0).fit_predict(Z)\nari = adjusted_rand_score(hidden_labels, clusters)  #TODO: the adjusted Rand index between hidden_labels and clusters\nprint(\"ARI:\", round(ari, 3))\npd.crosstab(clusters, hidden_labels, rownames=[\"cluster\"], colnames=[\"cultivar\"])",
    [("ari", "adjusted_rand_score(hidden_labels, clusters).")]),
  ],
  "further": ["Repeat the clustering on the first two PCA components only. Is the ARI better or worse?", "Try agglomerative clustering and draw a dendrogram with SciPy.", "What happens to the silhouette scores if you forget to standardise?"],
 },
